{"id":9359,"date":"2021-10-06T13:31:47","date_gmt":"2021-10-06T13:31:47","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/faq\/"},"modified":"2021-10-06T13:35:15","modified_gmt":"2021-10-06T13:35:15","slug":"faq","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/faq\/","title":{"rendered":"FAQ"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-page\" data-elementor-id=\"9359\" class=\"elementor elementor-9359 elementor-7632\" data-elementor-post-type=\"page\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-faf90f7 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"faf90f7\" data-element_type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-f9a471f\" data-id=\"f9a471f\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-f10a6cc elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"f10a6cc\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">Frequently Asked Questions<\/h2>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-fee2bcb elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"fee2bcb\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h5 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">Generally about molecular spectroscopy<\/h5>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-33d2c69 elementor-widget elementor-widget-accordion\" data-id=\"33d2c69\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"accordion.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-5431\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"1\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-5431\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">1. FT-IR, FT-NIR, Raman spectroscopy\u2026 What does it mean?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-5431\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"1\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-5431\"><p>All these methods consist in the interaction of a sample with electromagnetic radiation of one specific wavelength (Raman spectroscopy) or in a given interval (infrared spectroscopy) and we speak of them in general as methods of molecular spectroscopy. The output of this analysis is then the spectrum, which is unique for each compound, and from its changes it is possible to determine, among other things, a number of other physico-chemical properties of the sample. You can find <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/model-series\/raman-spectroscopy\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">classic and UV Raman spectroscopy<\/a>, infrared spectroscopy in the near (<a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/model-series\/nir-spectrometers\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NIR<\/a> or <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/model-series\/nir-spectrometers\/\">FT-NIR<\/a>), middle (<a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/model-series\/ft-ir-spectroscopy\/\">FT-IR<\/a>) or far (FAR-IR) region or <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/model-series\/libs-en\/\">LIBS<\/a>. <\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-5432\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"2\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-5432\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">2. What type of analysis can I perform?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-5432\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"2\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-5432\"><p>Raman and infrared spectrometers can be used for both <strong>qualitative<\/strong>analysis (<strong>identification<\/strong>and <strong>verification<\/strong>of substances) and <strong>quantitative<\/strong>measurements, including <strong>analysis of mixtures<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-5433\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"3\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-5433\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">3. What are the advantages of molecular spectroscopy?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-5433\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"3\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-5433\"><p>Molecular spectroscopy is a fast, reliable, non-invasive method that, in addition, usually does not require <strong>any sample modification<\/strong>. As a result, it saves you time, money and material, and you can perform sample analysis without deep knowledge.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-5434\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"4\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-5434\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">4. We have a Raman spectrometer in the laboratory. How can an FT-IR spectrometer help me?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-5434\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"4\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-5434\"><p>FT-IR and Raman spectroscopy are complementary methods, which means that samples that are not well measurable by FT-IR spectroscopy usually provide a strong Raman signal and vice versa. Raman spectroscopy is more suitable e.g. for <strong>measuring samples that contain water<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-5435\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"5\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-5435\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">5. How often are molecular spectroscopy methods used?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-5435\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"5\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-5435\"><p>Currently, infrared and Raman spectroscopy are used in all possible branches of science, research and industry, and IRS components are equipped with hand-held analyzers. <strong>More than 650 of our devices<\/strong>already operate in the Czech and Slovak Republic.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-b30e162 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"b30e162\" data-element_type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-8a02ec2\" data-id=\"8a02ec2\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ecd250f elementor-align-center elementor-widget elementor-widget-button\" data-id=\"ecd250f\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"button.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-button-wrapper\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-button elementor-button-link elementor-size-sm\" href=\"#elementor-action%3Aaction%3Dpopup%3Aopen%26settings%3DeyJpZCI6NzU0NSwidG9nZ2xlIjpmYWxzZX0%3D\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-button-content-wrapper\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"elementor-button-text\">I want to receive news from the world of molecular spectroscopy!<\/span>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/span>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-dbc8820 dce_masking-none elementor-widget elementor-widget-image\" data-id=\"dbc8820\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"image.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<figure class=\"wp-caption\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/product\/nanoram\/\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"768\" height=\"565\" src=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/01\/7173d73b-768x565.jpg\" class=\"attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-image-5718\" alt=\"Ru\u010dn\u00ed Raman\u016fv spektrometr NanoRam\" srcset=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/01\/7173d73b-768x565.jpg 768w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/01\/7173d73b-300x221.jpg 300w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/01\/7173d73b-1024x753.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/01\/7173d73b-1536x1130.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/app\/uploads\/2021\/01\/7173d73b.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" \/>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<figcaption class=\"widget-image-caption wp-caption-text\">Handheld Raman spectrometer NanoRam<\/figcaption>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/figure>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c16cf6c elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"c16cf6c\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h5 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">About your application and samples<\/h5>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-c7e59d2 elementor-widget elementor-widget-accordion\" data-id=\"c7e59d2\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"accordion.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-2091\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"1\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2091\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">1. What samples can I measure?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2091\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"1\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-2091\"><p>You can use molecular spectroscopy methods to analyze <strong>solid, liquid and gaseous samples, powder, gel, microscopic and large objects<\/strong> (eg wall frescoes), cells and inorganic samples and much more. The possibilities of these methods are indeed extensive.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-2092\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"2\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2092\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">2. How small or large samples can be measured?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2092\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"2\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-2092\"><p>Using our instruments, microscopic samples with a <strong>spatial resolution of only 10 nm<\/strong> (cells, trace amounts of substances i) as well as large samples such as <strong>wall frescoes or paintings<\/strong> can be measured.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-2093\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"3\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2093\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">3. I need to analyze a gaseous sample, is it possible?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2093\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"3\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-2093\"><p>Yes! Both FT-IR and Raman spectrometers can be equipped with gas cells, with which you can analyze <strong>gas samples<\/strong> similarly to samples in other states or forms.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-2094\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"4\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2094\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">4. My application is not in your list. Can I still use any of the devices?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2094\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"4\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-2094\"><p>These applications are just a modest choice from a <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/solutions\/\"><strong>myriad of molecular spectroscopy options<\/strong><\/a>. If you are interested in how you can use it to take your research, development or production processes to the next level, do not hesitate to contact us, we will be happy to advise you on everything.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-2095\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"5\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2095\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">5. My sample has strong fluorescence. What can be done with that?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2095\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"5\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-2095\"><p>If you are already measuring or want to measure with a Raman spectrometer, try a <strong>different wavelength of the excitation laser<\/strong>. Also, if appropriate for your sample, you can explore the possibilities of FT-IR spectroscopy. Contact us and we will advise you.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-2096\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"6\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2096\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">6. I need to measure the distribution of individual components of a larger sample, e.g. tablet. Is there a device that would help me with such a problem?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2096\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"6\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-2096\"><p>Yes! <strong>Dispersion Raman spectrometers DXR3 and DXR3xi<\/strong> are directly designed for mapping similarly large samples, with which you can <strong>map the tablet in a few tens of minutes<\/strong>, determine the distribution of individual sample components at each point, and even measure 3D chemical maps.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-2097\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"7\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2097\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">7. I usually analyze very similar samples. Can I make my work easier?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2097\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"7\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-2097\"><p>For such a case, it is possible to create a calibration method using the <strong>TQ Analyst<\/strong>program, with which you will receive your answer almost immediately.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-2098\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"8\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-2098\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">8. There is a lot of dust at our place, will it not hurt the device?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-2098\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"8\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-2098\"><p>In our offer you will also find spectrometers that are designed directly for demanding operations, both in terms of possible pollution, as well as high or low temperatures and other parameters.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element 