aceable lasers<\/strong>, <strong>filters<\/strong> and <strong>gratings<\/strong>, various measuring attachments for <strong>measuring tablets, bottles, samples in bags or tanks, autosamplers, fiber optics, integration spheres<\/strong> and much more depending on the instrument.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-accordion-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-title-1785\" class=\"elementor-tab-title\" data-tab=\"5\" role=\"button\" aria-controls=\"elementor-tab-content-1785\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"elementor-accordion-title\" tabindex=\"0\">5. Is it possible to combine molecular spectroscopy methods and other measuring techniques?<\/a>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div id=\"elementor-tab-content-1785\" class=\"elementor-tab-content elementor-clearfix\" data-tab=\"5\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"elementor-tab-title-1785\"><p>Molecular spectroscopy methods can be very well combined with a variety of techniques: <strong><a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/product\/raman-afm\/\">AFM<\/a>, <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/solutions\/science-research-education\/raman-sem-combined-microscopy\/\">SEM<\/a>, TERS, <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/product\/ftir-gc\/\">GC\/LC<\/a>, mass spectroscopy, <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/product\/combination-of-ft-ir-and-rheometer\/\">rheometry<\/a>, <a href=\"https:\/\/nicoletcz.cz\/en\/product\/ftir-tga\/\">TGA<\/a><\/strong> and others. In addition, Raman and infrared spectroscopy are complementary methods, so it is very advantageous to use both types of instruments in the analysis.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-d894b5a elementor-align-center elementor-widget elementor-widget-button\" data-id=\"d894b5a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"button.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-c